{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNzIxMTQ=","is_bot":false,"login":"zWaR","name":""},"body":"## Extension

`@webframp/gitlab` (2026.10.14.2)

## What I tried

A task had been created as a child of another work item, and I needed it to
stand on its own and show up on the team's issue board. That takes two
changes:

1. Remove its parent, so it has no ancestor.
2. Convert it from a Task to an Issue. Issue boards don't list Tasks, so a
   detached Task doesn't show up on the board.

## Expected vs. what happened

**Expected:** a method for each, like the existing `update_issue` and
`set_issue_assignees`.

**What happened:** no method covers either change. `update_issue` uses the
REST issues API, which can't change a work item's hierarchy or type. Both
are only available through the work-item GraphQL API. The only options were
the web UI or calling GraphQL outside swamp.

## Suggested fix

Two methods in `extensions/models/gitlab/projects.ts`, built on the existing
`graphqlRequest` helper:

- `remove_work_item_parent` (`project`, `iid`): detaches the work item from
  its parent, then re-reads the parent and fails if GitLab kept it. Does
  nothing when there's no parent.
- `convert_work_item_type` (`project`, `iid`, `type`): changes the type,
  e.g. Task to Issue. It matches `type` against the project's
  `workItemTypes`, ignoring case. An unknown name fails with the list of
  available types. Does nothing when the item already has that type.

Each writes a small resource (`workItemParent`, `workItemType`) recording
the state before and after.

The GraphQL behind it:

```graphql
query workItem($fullPath: ID!, $iid: String!) {
  project(fullPath: $fullPath) {
    workItems(iid: $iid) {
      nodes {
        id
        workItemType { name }
        widgets { ... on WorkItemWidgetHierarchy { parent { reference(full: true) } } }
      }
    }
    workItemTypes { nodes { id name } }
  }
}

mutation removeWorkItemParent($id: WorkItemID!) {
  workItemUpdate(input: { id: $id, hierarchyWidget: { parentId: null } }) {
    workItem { widgets { ... on WorkItemWidgetHierarchy { parent { reference(full: true) } } } }
    errors
  }
}

mutation convertWorkItem($id: WorkItemID!, $typeId: WorkItemsTypeID!) {
  workItemConvert(input: { id: $id, workItemTypeId: $typeId }) {
    workItem { workItemType { name } }
    errors
  }
}
```

The full change, with tests, README, release notes and a manifest bump, is
in a single commit on my fork. It follows the existing method and test
patterns, and all 212 tests pass:
https://github.com/zWaR/swamp-extensions/commit/4672cc19

Both mutations have run successfully against a self-managed GitLab Community
Edition (CE) instance.
The lookup query, with the hierarchy widget and `workItemTypes`, is only
covered by the mocked tests so far.

I'm happy for you to implement it however you like. Attribution would be
nice but isn't necessary. I'd also like to contribute code directly in
future, if that ever makes sense.
